  "title": "Warehouse and logistics",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "portuguese-for-work run, 2026-11-22: written by hand for Portugal (European Portuguese, pt-PT), not yet read by a human. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation (the 'German' tab). Words already in the lexicon, the IMT deck or another sector are refs, with this job's own example and sense. Working conditions, contracts and rules are general orientation only.",
  "intro": "Warehouses and distribution centres around Lisbon and Porto hire many newcomers, often through temporary work agencies. This deck has the warehouse and the machines, picking and packing, goods in and dispatch, safety, and the team and the agency. Everyone says tu, and many instructions come from a scanner or a screen.",
  "introEasy": "Do you work in a warehouse in Portugal? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Operador/a de armazém",
    "Preparador/a de encomendas",
    "Operador/a de empilhador",
    "Fiel de armazém",
    "Conferente"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "Driving a forklift (empilhador) needs training and the employer's authorisation. Never drive one just because someone asks you to.",
    "Count twice and say what is missing: «Faltam duas caixas nesta palete.» A mistake in an order costs more than a slow start.",
    "If you came through an agency (empresa de trabalho temporário), your employer is the agency: ask it for your contract, your payslips and your schedule. General orientation, not legal advice."
  ],
